    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance? mostly looking for stuff on color contrast ratios and making sure screen readers work right for a new fintech app we're building",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a quick checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance, specifically tailored for your fintech app's color contrast and screen reader accessibility.\n\n**Color Contrast & Visual Clarity**\n*   **AAA Level Contrast**: Ensure all text has a contrast ratio of at least **7:1** against its background (e.g., dark grey text on white).\n*   **AA Level Contrast**: For normal text (18pt+ or 14pt+ bold), aim for **4.5:1**; for large text (18pt+), aim for **3:1**.\n*   **UI Components**: Buttons, links, and input fields must meet these ratios, even if they are small.\n*   **Glints & Reflections**: Avoid shiny, reflective surfaces that can cause glare, as they often confuse screen readers and reduce contrast.\n*   **Red/Green Warnings**: Never rely solely on red or green to indicate errors or success states; always pair them with text labels or icons.\n*   **Glints & Reflections**: Avoid shiny, reflective surfaces that can cause glare, as they often confuse screen readers and reduce contrast.\n\n**Screen Reader & Keyboard Navigation",
      "source": "target",
