    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the list looks good so far. can u finish the screen reader part? also, what kind of specific 'bugs' or hidden issues should we look out for during testing that might mess up the accessibility?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the rest of the screen reader checklist and a list of hidden \"bugs\" to watch for during your fintech app testing.\n\n**Screen Reader & Keyboard Navigation (Continued)**\n*   **ARIA Labels**: Ensure every interactive element (buttons, icons, images) has a descriptive `aria-label` or `alt` text. Screen readers need to know *what* the button does, not just that it's a button.\n*   **Skip Links**: Implement a \"Skip to Main Content\" link at the top of the page so keyboard-only users can bypass repetitive navigation menus.\n*   **Focus Indicators**: Make sure the focus ring is visible and large enough for users with motor impairments. A faint blue outline is often too subtle.\n*   **Dynamic Content Updates**: If data loads dynamically (like transaction updates), ensure the screen reader announces the change (using `aria-live` regions) so users don't miss new financial alerts.\n*   **Form Error Handling**: When a user makes a mistake on a form (e.g., invalid card number), the screen reader must announce the specific error message clearly, not just say \"Error.\"\n*   **Glints & Reflections**: Avoid",
      "source": "target",
